---
// @ts-check
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../assets/leszek-portrait.webp';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — labs.walerys.app"
  description="I'm Leszek. Engineering global enterprise systems, making repetitive work disappear, and building across software and hardware."
  profile
>
  <article class="prose about">
    <h1 id="about">About</h1>
    <div class="about-intro">
      <div class="about-intro-copy">
        <p class="about-label">The person behind Labs</p>
        <p>
          I’m Leszek. I lead engineering teams behind global enterprise systems, where
          high availability and scalability are everyday requirements. Keeping services
          dependable around the clock shapes how I think about architecture, change,
          and the complexity we choose to take on.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="portrait">
        <div class="portrait-frame">
          <Image
            src={portrait}
            alt="Black-and-white portrait of Leszek, resting his chin on his hand."
            widths={[240, 480, 720]}
            sizes="(max-width: 540px) 240px, 208px"
            width={720}
            height={720}
            loading="eager"
            class="portrait-image"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption>Leszek / behind the labs</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p>
      At that scale, repetitive manual work is more than a nuisance — it is a source of
      operational risk. I appreciate a particular kind of engineering laziness: the
      willingness to do the hard work once so nobody has to keep doing the routine work.
      That instinct carries into my own experiments, too.
    </p>

    <h2 id="from-code-to-hardware">From code to hardware</h2>
    <p>
      That interest in what sits underneath started early. The day we brought home our
      first computer, I took it apart to see how the components matched what I’d read.
      It went back together with no screws left over — and left me wanting to understand
      both the machine and the code.
    </p>
    <p>
      At home, that curiosity extends into the walls. I built my smart home from the
      electrical installation up, bringing wiring, hardware, and software together as
      one system. Different scale, same instinct: follow the dependencies and understand
      how the whole thing works.
    </p>

    <h2 id="why-labs">Why labs?</h2>
    <p>
      Labs is my personal space for experiments and lessons that are worth keeping:
      software, hardware, automation, and better ways of working. Not a portfolio of
      polished answers, but a record of what I tried, what happened, and what I would
      change next time.
    </p>
    <p>
      Writing it down helps me think more clearly. Sharing it gives someone else a
      starting point — or a chance to show me what I missed.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 13rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-intro-copy {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .about-label {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .portrait {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .portrait-frame {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, calc(100% - 1.5rem) 0, 100% 1.5rem, 100% 100%, 0.75rem 100%, 0 calc(100% - 0.75rem));
  }

  .portrait-frame::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .portrait-image {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0;
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, calc(100% - 1.25rem) 0, 100% 1.25rem, 100% 100%, 0.5rem 100%, 0 calc(100% - 0.5rem));
  }

  .portrait figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .about-intro {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .portrait {
      width: min(15rem, 100%);
    }
  }
</style>
